    {
      "id": "zrs1plo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Characteristics of Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Plant classification covers structural variations, tissue organization, and cellular features.",
        "Photosynthesis is the fundamental process driving plant nutrition and energy production.",
        "Plant reproduction occurs through sexual mechanisms as well as vegetative propagation.",
        "Plant hormones regulate key growth responses, developmental stages, and physiological functions."
      ],
      "id": "hx52udv"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u8xglss",
      "content": "• Plants are multicellular eukaryotic organisms."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9nhnmeq",
      "content": "• They contain chlorophyll and perform photosynthesis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vsubc4o",
      "content": "• Cell walls are made of cellulose."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "57gf41z",
      "content": "• They are generally non‑motile."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m7bu9gl",
      "content": "• They store food mainly in the form of starch."
    },
    {
